# Copy to `.dev.vars` for `wrangler dev`. Never commit the copy.
#
# The public halves of the keys attach tickets may be signed with, as
# comma-separated lowercase hex. Its counterpart is the web Worker's
# TICKET_SIGNING_KEY — generate the pair together with the one-liner in
# `packages/web/.dev.vars.example` and put the *public* line here.
#
# **A list rather than one key.** Rotating a single key means deploying both
# Workers at the same instant, which two `wrangler deploy`s cannot be; with a
# list the new key goes here first, the mint switches to it, and the old one is
# removed afterwards, with no window in which a fresh ticket meets a relay that
# has never heard of the key that signed it.
#
# Leave it out and every attach is refused with 4401, which is the correct
# answer for a relay whose mint has not been set up.
TICKET_PUBLIC_KEYS="…"

# This relay's own Ed25519 seed, 64 lowercase hex characters. Its public half is
# the `relay_key` every control-link challenge carries, which a daemon pins
# across reconnects — so unlike TICKET_PUBLIC_KEYS this is the *private* half,
# and it is one key rather than a list. Rotating it is a re-pin on every machine
# in the fleet, which is why it is generated once and left alone:
#   node -e "console.log(Buffer.from(crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32))).toString('hex'))"
#
# Leave it out and every control link is refused with 4503 and an `unconfigured`
# error frame, which is the correct answer for a relay whose key has never been
# set up — as opposed to a startup check, which would take the Worker down.
RELAY_SIGNING_KEY="…"
